  "what_it_is": {
    "prose": "The Indian Air Force is the air arm of the Indian Armed Forces, established 8 October 1932. The IAF operates over 1,700 aircraft including Su-30MKI, MiG-29, Mirage 2000, Rafale, LCA Tejas, and Jaguar fighters; C-17, C-130J, IL-76, and An-32 transports; AH-64E Apache, Mi-17, CH-47F Chinook, and ALH Dhruv helicopters. The IAF also operates IAI Heron and Searcher UAVs, DRDO Tapas-BH, and is the lead service for the MQ-9B Predator-B procurement (16 of 31 aircraft). The IAF is a key customer for HAL, BEL, BDL, and TASL products.",
    "sources": [
      "src-01",
      "src-02",
      "src-03"
    ]
  },
